---
import IconGitHub from "@components/icons/IconGitHub.astro";
import ProjectSlide from "./project-slide.astro";
import Rune from "./Rune.svelte";
---

<style is:global>
  .whisper-world {
    --text-accent: var(--text-color);
  }
  .whisper-world .mosaic {
    grid-template-areas:
      "a a a a a"
      "a a a a a"
      "a a a a a"
      "a a a a a"
      "w w w r r";
  }

  .whisper-world .mosaic img {
    object-fit: fill;
  }
</style>

<ProjectSlide class="whisper-world">
  <Fragment slot="title">Whisper World</Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="year">2024</Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="description">
    WhisperWorld is a client-server chat app written in <code>C</code>, built to
    dive deeper into systems programming and TCP/IP. Powered by <code
      >libuv</code
    > for async I/O and <code>CMake</code> for builds, it gave me hands-on practice
    with memory management, networking, and modular design. The original idea was
    to rebuild it in other languages to compare ecosystems and approaches.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="tags">
    <span class="tag">C</span>
    <span class="tag">libuv</span>
    <span class="tag">CMake</span>
    <span class="tag">TCP/IP</span>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="highlights">
    <li>
      <span class="highlight">Built</span> a multi-client chat server and client in
      <code>C</code> with broadcasting and connection management.
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="highlight">Integrated</span>
      <code>libuv</code> for non-blocking, event-driven I/O, replacing the initial
      <code>select()</code> implementation.
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="highlight">Migrated</span> build setup from a simple
      <code>Makefile</code> to <code>CMake</code> with auto-fetched dependencies and
      cross-platform support.
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="highlight">Explored</span> edge cases like partial reads, oversize
      payloads, and connection drops, while planning next steps such as an event queue
      and custom protocol abstraction.
    </li>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="footer">
    <a
      title="Dig in the code on Github"
      class="icon-link"
      aria-label="Whisper World GitHub repo"
      rel="noopener"
      href="https://github.com/alezen9/whisper-world-c"
      target="_blank"
    >
      <IconGitHub class:list={["animate", "icon-github"]} />
    </a>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="mosaic">
    <figure class="tilt main" style="grid-area: a;" title="Local chat example">
      <img
        src="/projects/whisper-world/a.webp"
        alt="Whisper World - Local chat example"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </figure>
    <Rune client:load className="ansuz" />
    <p class="caption">
      <span class="name">Ansuz</span>
      <span>Sky father's mark </span>
      <span>Noise shaping the frame</span>
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ProjectSlide>
